+# Independent channel coordinator trial
+
+This isolated pilot owns preparation and dispatch for one prepared RoomEQ
+channel. It uses checked `PreparedChannelInput` accessors and the shared IIR,
+FIR, mixed-crossover, target, preprocessing, recovery and assembly kernels in
+`roomeq-engine`. It owns no filesystem access, artifact store, CLI, report shell,
+networking or duplicated DSP algorithms.
+
+Workflow prepares resources and calls `channel_execution`. The engine does not
+depend on this coordinator, including through dev dependencies. The trial moves
+the former `roomeq_engine::channel_execution` public entry points here; this is
+an explicit API migration, not a compatibility reexport or a landed decision.
+The prepared-state fields remain private. Shared engine operations expose the
+existing checked usable-curve selector and preference-filter construction.
+
+Ten coordinator tests retain their module and test names. One cross-boundary
+FIR test moves here with its original name and unchanged numeric assertions;
+its fixture remains owned by the engine and is included from the original
+source path. Test-only setup helpers are copied without changing inputs.
+The logical engine scope remains 972 cases across the two physical targets,
+with the same two ignored cases. A leaf-only run covers 11 cases and cannot
+stand in for the full engine scope.
+
+Acceptance requires controlled before/after build-plus-execution and memory
+measurements, mapped owning and affected-consumer tests, numerical and coverage
+checks, a complete supported API/consumer audit, and an explicit maintenance
+tradeoff. This pilot has not been accepted or copied into the refactor worktree.
